    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0404" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/6–2249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-22">June 22,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received June 22—6:02 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1346. Local press June 20 reports Chang Lan, Shih Liang, Lo Lung-chi, “Wang
                    Pao-chang, Kuo Chen-tao,<anchor n="38" xml:id="d466-f1"/> others arrived in
                    Nanking June 19 on way to Peiping. Chang, Lo, Shih, press states, aside from
                    attending preparatory committee of new PCC will also attend fourth plenary
                    session of Democratic League.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Peiping 231, Shanghai 739, OffEmb Canton
                    unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d466-f1" n="38" xml:id="d466-f1-content">
                <p>All Democratic League members; they reached Peiping on June 24.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
